cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Monologue or Dialogue? Measuring Conversational Structure in the
  Reasoning Traces of Large Language Models
message: If you use this work, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Oskar
    family-names: Engl
    email: oskar.engl@ik.me
    affiliation: Johannes Kepler University Linz
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/oskarengl/dialogic-multiplicity-in-reasoning-traces
abstract: >-
  Reasoning models such as DeepSeek-R1 produce a long stretch of intermediate
  tokens before they answer. Although each stretch is written by a single model
  in one pass, one can observe in a trace that questions receive answers,
  objections receive concessions, and the argument turns against itself and
  starts again. This study asks whether a reasoning trace's textual shape is
  more akin to a monologue or to a dialogue, using three text-analysis methods
  that must first prove themselves on four corpora of known voice structure.
keywords:
  - reasoning traces
  - large language models
  - stylometry
  - conversation analysis
  - style change detection
  - dialogue acts
license: MIT
date-released: '2026-08-05'
